 talks about  this but i found this to be a huge deal  in real world use apple has been great  at being able to nudge you about  notifications without other people  hearing but i found that sometimes it is  just too weak the same thing goes for  using it as an alarm to wake me up who  knows maybe i'm just a lot less  sensitive to the vibrations compared to  other people but one thing is for sure  the series 7 has a much stronger tactic  engine then my series 5 and the earlier  apple watches and after using this for a  week and then putting on my series 5 for  today it is a substantial difference  this makes me want to start using it as  my daily alarm which i rarely used  before and that along with the faster  charging and better battery life will  likely push me over that edge apple  really focused on the faster charging  feature with this watch and that just  eight minutes gets you a full night of  sleep tracking and that the watch  charges 33 faster as well now battery  life has always been an issue with apple  watches and though most of the time i  can get through a full day some days  when i'm really using it more my series  5 will die before bedtime when i saw  that apple quoted the same 18 hours of  battery life i was disappointed  especially after they said that the  screen is 50 percent thicker i thought  how often do people break their screens  i am super tough on mine and is never  been an issue it's been super strong but  many people complain about battery life  so much so that people will actually go  and disable the always-on displays to  help so why not use the extra space for  a bigger battery instead of a thicker  screen well it turns out that apple did  increase the battery capacity with these  new watches the 41 millimeter has the  biggest improvement but it is still  there with the 45 millimeter that with  the fact that the chip is more efficient  than my s5 and this watch is brand new  made a noticeable difference in battery  life and now that we have fast charging  i will end up using sleep tracking as  well  now the other big thing they pushed is  the display at first glance it seemed  nothing like the 20 larger that they  talk about and their product images show  online on their website i found that it  really depends on what apps and which  watch faces you use some have almost no  difference but others are very  noticeable in reality the biggest screen  is not a reason to upgrade but apple's  software limitations might actually be  now i personally really like the new  contour face which is designed to  maximize the screen size and really show  that off and it uses the light  refraction from the curved glass of the  screen now sure they could have added  this to the 44 millimeter models from  the past but it wouldn't look as cool so  i understand why they might not want to  do that but the modular duo watch face  is a serious ripoff this phase allows  for two full width really detailed  complications like stocks for example  and none of that info bends into the  screen curve like with the contour face  so why not add a ever so slightly  smaller version for the older watches  well like i said this is a rip off i  think it's just so that people would  have another reason to upgrade now of  course we do have the world time and the  portrait watch faces which are available  on older models and they look good but  once i got used to the larger screen of  the seven compared to my five they  looked uh quite a bit smaller on the  five especially the portrait one now i  also noticed a few other differences  that apple didn't mention with the  display one is contrast where the series  seven has much less reflectivity and  better contrast than my five which is a  great thing and the other one of course  is the brighter display when it is  dimmed i hated that with my five like i  said it was my biggest disappointment  and the six it promised two and a half  times brighter display when it is dimmed  but it turned out that that was only  outdoors if it is very sunny and  personally if i'm outdoors i'm not  trying to slowly kind of glance down my  watch and see the time i can move around  a lot more freely now the 7 promises to  be 70 brighter and the key thing is  indoors when the watch is dimmed and  that is definitely noticeable especially  with particular watch faces the portrait  watch face shows almost no difference  but more minimal ones like california  are dramatically brighter it's almost  like the series 7 doesn't even dim or it  barely dims when you're using this apple  thank you for finally fixing this listen  to my complaints from years ago and  making the always-on display much more  useful now onto the final software  features that make a big real world  difference and that is the keyboard now  i'm not sure about you guys but i hated  typing or to be more accurate scratching  or sketching on the screen with the  apple watch in order to write something  it is so slow annoying that i ended up  never really using this and i relied on  voice which does work well but it is not  always possible for example in loud  situations or when you need to be quiet  well we now have this new full keyboard  with swiping that actually works quite  well once you get used to it once again  i do think that they could have made  this work on a 44 millimeter watch but  of course apple is not giving that to us  these legitimate upgrades and software  limitations with the six might actually  make it worth upgrading from a six to a  seven if money is not an issue for you  at all but for most people you shouldn't  do it now coming from a 5 though where  your battery was worse from the start  and it is now wearing out like mine is  at for example 86 capacity it's now a  way more logical thing to upgrade to a 7  than i thought at the launch of this  watch and of course for series 4 owners  it's an even bigger upgrade the main  question is if you should wait for the  series 8 which will almost certainly be  fully redesigned well if you're on a  budget and you only upgrade your watch  every 3 to 5 years i would say try to  wait another year if you can  now if you upgrade more often or if you  might not like the upcoming square edge  design i say go for it by the series 7.  the improvements are a lot bigger than i  expected at the launch of this watch and  overall the series 7 is a much more  useful upgrade than i thought before at  least for me personally if you are  wondering how the se compares to the 7  go ahead and check out our full  comparison right over there and click  above to subscribe if you guys want to  help us reach our goal of 1 million  subscribers and to see more videos like  this one this has been max and i will  see you in the next video
 

